A||||4||Cozmo||does water wetter work?||||5||
Z||000000||Cozmo||05-28-2001||07:25 PM||||While waiting for the counter person at Discount Auto Parts to get me some stuff I noticed some Red Line water wetter <A HREF="http://www.redlineoil.com/redlineoil/wwti.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.redlineoil.com/redlineoil/wwti.htm</A> <BR>I don't usually believe in that "mechanic in a can" crapola but after reading the website it actually looks like it could work...<BR>Anyone tried this stuff or is it just more "snake oil"?<BR>C02M0||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mach10||05-28-2001||07:34 PM||||Sounds pretty hokey. By the same "surface tension" logic, you could say that adding some dish detergent to a full water mix would cool better, 'cos soap will do that... I don't trust it.||||reg||13
Z||000002||theogre||05-28-2001||08:01 PM||||A wetting agent can help, how much is questionable. If the OE cooling system is working properly then you probably won't notice much diferance. If you've got some corrosion buildup the stuff may improve things at least temporarily. (A corroded system really needs cleaning...) It won't hurt anything to try it. It's used in allot of race setups and it does do what it says. It's pretty popular stuff. It would probably help a V6 or V8 more tha a 4 cyl.<P>I don't use it myself. My cooling system is clean and I've not had any sign of overheating at all since replacing the heatercore last year.<P>Laugh at Wetting agents if you want. They do work in the applications they are designed for. There's one that used to be called FireOut that is/was used by fire departments to make the water cling to what ever was burning. I met the guy that invented that one. I put a new sterio in his Vette... <P>The analogy to soap/detergent is correct, but no, you could not put detergent in the cooling system and get the same result.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||05-28-2001||09:59 PM||||I've used it in a few V-8 swaps mostly as a precautionary measure. My old '58 Jeep (chevy V8) started overheating when I put a K&N filter on it, and I couldn't get the fuel mixture back to where it would run cool. The 40 below seemed to help a little before I switched to EFI and a paper filter. <P>JTR (Jags that run) recomends the stuff with their Jaguar and S-10 V8 conversions, that's when I first started using it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cozmo||05-29-2001||08:59 AM||||I did some more research, the stuff seems to do what it advertises.  The computer overclockers are using it in their hot-rodded water cooled boxes and seeing 10-20 degree drops.<BR>So I went ahead and bought some, ($7) and "got bit by the snake" <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>I'll post some comments after I've run the car a few days (I put it in the 2M6 Targa).<BR><B>C02M0</B><BR>||||reg||14
